00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:06.150 align:start position:0%
it has been more than two years since  nba superstar kobe bryant his 13 year  old daughter gianna and seven others  were killed in a helicopter crash now a  lawsuit filed by bryant's wedding widow  that's vanessa bryan has gone to trial  in los angeles she accuses police and  firefighters of sharing graphic photos  of the crash part of what her lawyer  told the court was a culture of  callousness  our national correspondent jerica duncan  has more on this story  years after l.a county officials took  pictures of victims remains in the hills  of calabasas california including kobe  bryant and his daughter gianna a trial  centered on law enforcement's conduct is  underway vanessa bryant was visibly  emotional during wednesday's proceedings  crying frequently in a dramatic opening  statement her attorney claimed law  enforcement exploited the accident by  taking and sharing pictures of kobe and  gianna as souvenirs  bryant's attorney also told jurors the  photos were virtual gossip and played  security video of an off-duty sheriff's  deputy showing them to a bartender to  support that claim an attorney for the  county said the footage marked a  regrettable moment of weakness and said  that site photography is an essential  tool for first responders to share  potentially life-saving information  though the sheriff previously admitted  that deputies had no place to take  photographs of bryant's remains brian's  lawsuit alleges the photos circulated  among 28 sheriff department devices and  at least a dozen firefighters but the  county's attorney defended leadership's  response pointing out that the photos  have never appeared publicly and calling  it a function of how diligent  authorities were at the time the sheriff  contained the photo spread by making  involved parties delete them rather than  conducting a formal investigation as a  result bryant's attorney claimed photos  could still be in circulation  bryant voiced that concern last year in  court documents writing for the rest of  my life one of two things will happen  either close up photos of my husbands  and daughters bodies will go viral  online or i will continue to live in  fear of that happening for cbs mornings  i'm jerica duncan  i hope those photos never become public  i like the i think it's interesting that  they said a regrettable moment of  weakness that doesn't make any sense to  me it doesn't doesn't make any sense  callousness exactly  that's what that is  and i think about vanessa and her family  now having to relive that as they're  sitting on in the courtroom  talking about this again especially in  the day and age where one leaked photo  can travel around the world just like  that
 

